---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Local Directory"
  description="Dining, retail, and fitness across MBR City's communities — District One, Meydan, Sobha Hartland, and Riviera — not just inside one of them."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Local directory</p>
    <h1>What's available district-wide</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Coverage varies a lot by community — some are still filling in retail,
      others have had years to mature. This page is the district-level view;
      for Riviera's promenade specifically, its own
      <a href="https://riviera.dst.llc/local-directory/">local directory</a>
      goes into more detail than makes sense to duplicate here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Retail and dining</h2>
    <p>
      Meydan One Mall is the district's main retail anchor — cinema,
      dining, and a large-format mall experience most individual
      communities don't have on their own. District One and Sobha Hartland
      residents typically drive to it or to Downtown/Business Bay for
      anything beyond community-level convenience retail. Riviera is the
      exception: its ground-floor promenade covers a meaningful amount of
      day-to-day dining and convenience shopping without leaving the
      development.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Fitness and outdoor</h2>
    <p>
      District One's defining feature here is the track around the Crystal
      Lagoon — a genuinely well-used running and cycling loop that draws
      people from other MBR City communities, not just District One
      residents. Meydan has its own cycling and running infrastructure tied
      to the racecourse grounds. Most residential buildings across the
      district also include their own gym as a standard amenity.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Callout kind="warn">
    This page describes what's typically available at the district level —
    specific tenants and venues change as communities continue to build out.
    Confirm current details directly rather than relying on this page alone.
  </Callout>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
